archmage84 wrote:
>
> But is 5 luck such a huge loss?

It is if you're in a crowd of nasties and you have to fight your way
out just to be able to run away to heal.  It is if you're playing
atheist so you don't have the option of a sacrifest at an nearby altar. 
It is if you have not yet found an altar.  If it if you've killed not
one but 3 shopkeepers so your luck is maxed out in the negative
direction and you have to fight past something stronger than a newt but
you can't hit it no matter how many times you swing.

Most of those situations don't happen in any one game, but the point
remains.  You do need to have planned it out to be able to pay the price
to make it up before you decide to start taking out shopkeepers.

> Don't you recover it automatically?

Too slowly unless you can do a sacrifest at a nearby altar.  There's
also the possibility of a dumb mistake - Do it before blessing your
luckstone because you're in a rush and didn't think of that and your
luck stays low until you do a sacrifest or die.  It's a mistake I
remember making rather a long time ago.


